  "evidence_interpretation": {
    "original_counterexamples": "Eleven valid failures at parent source using a separate real native PostgreSQL database per scenario. The earlier shared-history run had ten failures and one vacuous positive; the URL-form isolation fixture initially failed setup, then was corrected before the eleven-counterexample run.",
    "implementation_iterations": [
      "Initial account view incorrectly referenced the single-cycle software_stops field; corrected to the actual account broker mode.",
      "Expiry case also expired its lease when invoking the actor directly; corrected to the actual service loop renewal, preserving the real lease-lost refusal.",
      "A bare component-only bar pipeline has no native lease or policy; preserve that component contract while built production actors always renew and process signed recovery."
    ],
    "staged_hardening": "After the initial account path worked, two real key-retirement/PEM failures, an unresolved-order risk snapshot failure, and four invalid-fill-price failures in the new history fold were reproduced and fixed. They are not labeled original parent counterexamples.",
    "transport": "Actual paired gateway, real P256 approval, signed Commander HTTP handlers, native journal and running account actor; HTTP transport is in-process. No deployed host, phone CryptoObject or broker effect is claimed.",
    "atomicity": "Real PostgreSQL rollback before commit and lost reply after actual commit; original operation readback and exactly one effect confirmed.",
    "faults": "Fourteen independent controls pass; all fourteen introduced semantic regressions fail assertions with no collection/setup errors or skips; source restored exactly."
  },
